cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived KIN-SYS Protocol release."
title: "KIN-SYS Protocol: Provider-Neutral Governed Execution Prototype"
authors:
  - family-names: Kagoro
    given-names: Joel
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/joe933212-pixel/KIN-SYS-PROTOCOL"
abstract: >-
  KIN-SYS is a provider-neutral protocol architecture for governing and
  verifying digital instructions across institutional and jurisdictional
  boundaries. This research/reference release extends the MINAH-first governed
  execution prototype with institutional deployment and lifecycle registries,
  tenant-scoped authority grants, receiver-controlled trust and signed
  federation, provider-neutral OIDC identity adapter contracts, PostgreSQL-
  backed federation inbox/outbox and replay controls, and cross-installation
  reference tests. It includes reproducible conformance evidence and explicit
  security limitations. It is not a production deployment: identity providers,
  legal-source verification, institutional evidence, key custody and
  deployment infrastructure still require institution-specific integration.

keywords:
  - governed execution
  - institutional coordination
  - verifiable execution
  - distributed systems
  - digital sovereignty
  - protocol architecture
  - East Africa
